{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvanBesVHdrxUy3xcJTg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Recommendation: don't make the non-buyer survey the basis for the decision. Reshape the next step.**\n\n**Why the survey is weak evidence**\n- Stated willingness to pay is unreliable. People say a lower price would work far more often than they then buy.\n- Non-buyers mostly never considered the offer. They'll say \"cheaper\" because it's the easy answer.\n- Response bias will skew the results toward people who are already engaged.\n\n**What the data already says**\n- A 10x miss (0.3% against 3%) is unlikely to be closed by price alone. Halving the price would need an implausibly large lift in demand.\n- The 40% refund rate matters more than the take-up. People who wanted it enough to pay then changed their minds. That points to value or expectation problems, such as unclear promise, poor onboarding or accidental purchase. A lower price doesn't fix those.\n- The numbers are small. If roughly 10,000 customers saw the offer, that's about 30 buyers and about 12 refunds, so about 18 retained. Treat every rate as imprecise.\n\n**Cheaper, more informative steps first**\n1. Ask the refunders why, using their refund reasons and a short interview.\n2. Check whether the offer was seen, where it was placed and how it was worded.\n3. Segment buyers and non-buyers by recent support contact. Demand may exist only in a narrow group.\n4. Use the control group to see whether buyers' support usage or satisfaction actually changed.\n\n**If price is still the main hypothesis**\nRun a small randomised price test, for example £7 and £10, aimed at customers with recent support contacts. Agree the kill and proceed thresholds beforehand, including a net-of-refunds take-up rate.\n\n**Decision:** investigate. Don't commit to a lower price yet, and don't kill the add-on until the refund reasons are known."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3448,"cache_read_input_tokens":5010,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3448},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"87efd3df-1439-4522-9fcb-91c39e07cbc4","uuid":"a7f0041d-d221-4e81-b75e-21f716b5091a","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:10:03.675Z","request_id":"req_011CfvanBPzqATQkRGfEV8mQ"}
